    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0005-n0020-l0000",
      "p0005-n0020-l0001"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      5
    ],
    "text": "4.1.1 Rafts can only be on the water during daylight"
  },
  {
    "block_id": "b000033",
    "issues": [],
    "kind": "prose",
    "repairs": [
      {
        "left": "p0005-n0021-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0005-n0022-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0005-n0022-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0005-n0023-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0005-n0023-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0005-n0024-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0005-n0024-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0005-n0025-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0005-n0025-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0005-n0026-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0005-n0026-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0005-n0027-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0005-n0027-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0005-n0028-l0000"
      },
      {
        "left": "p0005-n0028-l0000",
        "operation": "line_wrap_to_space",
        "right": "p0005-n0029-l0000"
      }
    ],
    "section_id": "s0007",
    "source_line_ids": [
      "p0005-n0021-l0000",
      "p0005-n0022-l0000",
      "p0005-n0023-l0000",
      "p0005-n0024-l0000",
      "p0005-n0025-l0000",
      "p0005-n0026-l0000",
      "p0005-n0027-l0000",
      "p0005-n0028-l0000",
      "p0005-n0029-l0000"
    ],
    "source_pages": [
      5
    ],
    "text": "Allowing travel at night increases the carrying capacity of the river, but is impractical because whitewater rafting relies on visibility to remain safe. We have therefore chosen to only allow rafts on the water during daylight hours. For the purpose of this problem, daylight hours are de\ufb01ned as the civil twilight hours and daytime. Therefore the day begins when the center of the sun is 6 \u25e6below the horizon (the beginning of civil twilight). The day ends when the center of the sun is 6 \u25e6below the horizon (the end of civil dusk). This is the same de\ufb01nition that the FAA uses to regulate when aircraft are required to use lights, and provides an upper limit on the travel time of each boat [1]. Rafts that end up on the water after sunset will be monitored and used to show that river is above its carrying capacity."
  }
